  "notes": "{異|こと}なる means to differ or vary—a formal/written alternative to {違|ちが}う.\n\nREGISTER:\n- {違|ちが}う: to be different (everyday speech)\n- {異|こと}なる: to differ (formal, written, academic)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- AはBと{異|こと}なる: A differs from B\n- ～によって{異|こと}なる: varies depending on ~\n- ～とは{異|こと}なり: unlike ~, differing from ~\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {異|い}{文化|ぶんか}: different culture\n- {異|い}{常|じょう}: abnormal\n- {異|い}{議|ぎ}: objection\n- {相違|そうい}: difference (formal noun)\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nOften used in academic writing, news, and formal contexts where {違|ちが}う would sound too casual.",
